:false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"collaborators_only","topics":[],"visibility":"private","forks":0,"open_issues":15,"watchers":0,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"body":"Testing and CI, step 2.5. Six roles on two AlmaLinux versions is too large for one change, so it is split into one sub-issue per role. It is part of a testing standard for every repository: new and changed code is 100% covered, each repository keeps a coverage floor that only rises, mutation testing runs on every change where a tool exists, and configuration with its own test format needs a test for every rule.\n\n## What changes\n\nRoles have only ever been proven on the real servers, which is where several bugs were first found. Give each of the six roles a Molecule scenario run through the shared Molecule checks: containers with systemd running, the role applied twice with no changes the second time, and a verify that checks exact values as the account the real service runs as. What only a real server can show stays with the live verifies after deploy, and each role's scenario names what it can't test.\n\n## Done when\n\nevery role's scenario passes in CI on both AlmaLinux versions.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sh4i-yurei/keepbreathing-infra/issues/58/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sh4i-yurei/keepbreathing-infra/issues/58/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}